# Data and experiment artifacts — never committed.
#
# The leading slash matters and is not decoration: an unanchored `data/`
# matches a directory named `data` at ANY depth, which silently excluded the
# whole of `configs/data/` -- including `brats.yaml` (without which Hydra
# cannot compose at all, since configs/config.yaml lists `defaults: - data:
# brats`) and `splits.yaml` (the frozen record of which cases back every
# reported number). Both were missing from GitHub entirely, so a fresh clone
# could not run. Anchor directory rules that mean "the one at the repo root".
/data/
/outputs/
/checkpoints/
/wandb/

# These stay unanchored on purpose -- preprocessed arrays and NIfTI volumes
# are artifacts wherever they appear. Note this means a test fixture must not
# be committed as .npy.
*.npy
*.nii.gz

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Environments
.venv/
venv/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
